{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_012gcMvjbmvMtWEU6oU5KcqF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Anchor â€” what it is\n\n- **A single-folder personal productivity system** for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, no siblings). Plain-markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files under `domains/`) are the source of truth â€” no database, no binary formats.\n\n- **Its core app is `anchor_gui.py`** â€” a stdlib-only Python HTTP server that renders an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777` and writes task changes straight back to the markdown. It runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor` on the host `PUTER`/`gwl-server`. `anchor.py` is a CLI mirror of the same logic that also generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It manages a GTD-style task lifecycle** â€” Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored â€” across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing), with capture-to-inbox, priorities, energy levels, due dates, and notes. A daily `anchor_healthcheck.py` self-test runs at 5 AM via Task Scheduler.\n\n- **On top of that it ships an \"R&D Control Surface\"** â€” a per-project cockpit that runs the trio of skills (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman) as durable, isolated, server-side sessions. This has been built and merged through four versions:\n  - **v2:** session model, cached/validated summaries, Grass-Catcher idea lane, deliverable pinning, an interactive stream-json terminal REPL.\n  - **v3 \"Mission Control\":** real ConPTY terminals (the one declared `pywinpty` exception to the stdlib-only rule), per-session git-worktree isolation, a stacking window manager, stage handoffs, runnable deliverable previews (port-guarded â‰  8777), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n  - **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (merged 2026-06-13, commit `38fd70e`): lane tiles with status lights, inline expanding panels, an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), per-lane doc roles, a cost/tokens/time rollup, grass-idea promotion, and type-aware deliverable launch â€” and it fixes the v2 repeating-prompt terminal bug by loading each lane's skill exactly once.\n\n- **Its design intent (locked North Star):** make each project's window a calm, single-screen cockpit where every lane shows its latest session as a tile with one honest status light, clicking expands an in-place panel (summary on top, real resizable terminal below), and opening a session feels exactly like a normal Claude Code / Gemini session.\n\nThe defining constraint throughout: **stdlib-only Python, markdown as truth, everything accessible from any CLI** â€” with `pywinpty` as the single, explicitly-declared native exception for the terminal subsystem."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c95dab1-aa32-48d9-b3ba-92c042c5b7c9","uuid":"a32808e7-1bc3-41c6-a82a-055c49a34c4c","request_id":"req_011Cc1hEjDEiBaugGgJRMQj1"}
